---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy · Leonna’s travel journal"
  description="Plain-language details about local saves and privacy-first visitor analytics."
>
  <SiteHeader active="privacy" />

  <main id="main-content" class="collection-page">
    <header class="collection-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Visitor privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
      <p>This journal collects only the limited information needed to understand whether the site works well.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-sections">
      <section aria-labelledby="analytics-title">
        <h2 id="analytics-title">Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Each public page loads Cloudflare’s cookie-free Web Analytics beacon. It reports page views,
          visits, page-load timing and Core Web Vitals, plus aggregated dimensions such as country,
          page path, referring site, device type, browser, operating system, and navigation type.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare says it does not track people across websites. Query strings and custom events are
          not collected, so search and filter choices are not reported. Unsampled beacon data is kept
          for seven days before longer-term aggregation; the dashboard provides up to six months of
          analytics history.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="local-title">
        <h2 id="local-title">What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>
          Saved-place identifiers are stored only in your browser’s local storage. There is no reader
          account, public login, cloud profile, newsletter, advertising tracker, or public upload form.
          Clearing this site’s browser storage removes saved places from that browser.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
        <h2 id="hosting-title">Hosting and external links</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare hosts the public site and necessarily processes normal web requests to deliver it.
          Links to other websites have their own privacy practices. The journal does not use advertising
          trackers and does not sell visitor data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes-title">
        <h2 id="changes-title">Questions and changes</h2>
        <p>
          This notice was last updated on 14 November 2026. If the site adds accounts, advertising, or
          different analytics later, this page must be updated before those features go live. Privacy
          questions can be sent to Leonna through the same channel where this journal link was shared.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
